1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,343
Book Three, Proposition Eleven.

2
00:00:02,343 --> 00:00:13,946
If two circles touch one another internally, and their centers be taken, the straight line joining their centers, if it be also produced, will fall on the point of contact of the circles.

3
00:00:13,946 --> 00:00:23,997
Let the two circles A B C and A D E touch one another internally at the point A, and let the center F of circle A B C, and the center G of circle A D E, be taken.

4
00:00:23,997 --> 00:00:28,650
We claim that the straight line joined from G to F and produced falls on A.

5
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:41,160
For suppose it does not, but, if possible, let it fall outside as F G H, meeting the inner circle at D and the outer circle at H, and let the radii A F and A G be joined.

6
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:53,138
In triangle A F G, by One Twenty, any two sides are greater than the remaining side, so A G and G F together are greater than F A—that is, greater than the outer radius F H.

7
00:00:53,138 --> 00:00:59,686
Subtracting the common segment F G from each, the remainder A G is greater than the remainder G H.

8
00:00:59,686 --> 00:01:04,429
But A G and G D are radii of the inner circle A D E, so A G equals G D.

9
00:01:04,429 --> 00:01:10,242
Therefore G D is greater than G H—the part greater than the whole, which is impossible.

10
00:01:10,242 --> 00:01:17,190
Therefore, the line joined from F through G cannot fall outside the point of contact; it must fall on A.

11
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,860
As was required to prove.

12
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:26,269
Proposition Three Eleven establishes the collinearity of centers and point of contact for internally tangent circles.

13
00:01:26,269 --> 00:01:43,294
As Heath and Camerer observe, Euclid's diagram places G D inside G H along the line of centers because the inner circle lies wholly within the outer circle; combined with Three Seven, G H is the minimum segment from G to the outer circle, immediately forbidding G D from exceeding G H.

14
00:01:43,294 --> 00:01:55,600
In the GEOMETOR G-Index, node G one hundred nine connects Definition Three Three—circles touching without cutting—with the radius invariants of Book One, preparing the ground for Proposition Three Thirteen.

